                    "What are pre-press services?",
                    "Pre-press services prepare and check design files before printing. They help identify issues with layout, images, colour, fonts and production settings that could affect the printed result."
                ],
                [
                    "What is included in professional pre-press services?",
                    "Typical checks include page size, bleed and trim, image resolution, font handling, colour mode, overprint settings and print-ready PDF preparation. The exact checks depend on your printer&#039;s specifications and the job."
                ],
                [
                    "How long does the pre-press process take?",
                    "Timing depends on the number of files, pages or packaging variants and the corrections required. We review the supplied artwork and production specifications before confirming a turnaround."
                ],
                [
                    "What software is used for pre-press?",
                    "Adobe Acrobat Pro, InDesign, Illustrator and Photoshop are commonly used for checking, adjusting and preparing print files. The tools depend on the artwork format and production requirements."
                ],
                [
                    "What industries use pre-press services?",
                    "Businesses producing packaging, labels, catalogues, books, magazines, marketing collateral and other printed materials can benefit from pre-press checks before production."
                ],
                [
                    "Do I need pre-press services for digital printing?",
                    "Yes, digital printing also requires correctly prepared files. Resolution, page size, trim, bleed, fonts and colour settings should match the print provider&#039;s specifications to reduce preventable output issues."
